      "problem": "The coefficient of ${x}^{22}$ in the expansion of ${(3+{x}^{2})}^{13}$ is",
      "worked_solution": "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\frac{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\frac{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\frac{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+\u2026+(\\frac{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(3+{x}^{2})}^{13},$ we have $a=3,$ $b={x}^{2},$ and $n=13.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(3+{x}^{2})}^{13}=(\\frac{13}{0}){3}^{13}{({x}^{2})}^{0}+(\\frac{13}{1}){3}^{13-1}{({x}^{2})}^{1}+(\\frac{13}{2}){3}^{13-2}{({x}^{2})}^{2}+\u22ef+(\\frac{13}{13}){3}^{13-13}{({x}^{2})}^{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the ${x}^{22}$ term must be\n\n$$\n(\\frac{13}{11}){3}^{13-11}{({x}^{2})}^{11}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying this term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{13}{11}){3}^{13-11}{({x}^{2})}^{11} & =78\\cdot {3}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{22} \\\\  & =78\\cdot 9\\cdot {x}^{22} \\\\  & =702{x}^{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${x}^{22}$ is $702.$",
